# Secrets
#
# The glob covers .env.local, .env.production and every other spelling, because
# the one that leaks is always the spelling nobody thought to list. .env.example
# is deliberately allowed back: it holds names and no values.
.env*
!.env.example

# Raw export archives: these contain your full account data.
#
# data/raw/ is where the export is meant to be unzipped, but nothing forces that
# and an export unzipped anywhere else is the same data. The CSV rule is what
# actually protects it: diary.csv, reviews.csv, watchlist.csv and, above all,
# profile.csv, which holds the account's email address and which backfill.py
# refuses to read for exactly that reason. No CSV belongs in this repository.
data/raw/
*.csv
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# Caches
data/cache/tmdb.sqlite
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Wrangler's local state.
#
# Not build output: it stores the Cloudflare account id and the account's
# display name, which is the owner's email address. Deploying once writes it,
# and it was committed that way. The weekly workflow passes the account id as a
# secret and needs none of this.
.wrangler/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Local preview config
.claude/
